ency between the XR “click” and the neural stimulation.","position":{"start":{"line":71,"column":1},"end":{"line":71,"column":1}},"key":"HkOzEhqS6h"}],"key":"qsjT40H48T"}],"key":"da6te32fIJ"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":72,"column":1},"end":{"line":73,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Visual-Neural Sync: The XR environment (syGlass) ensures that the visual representation of the brain matches the physical stimulation site with micrometer precision, preventing “misfires” in sensitive brain regions.","position":{"start":{"line":72,"column":1},"end":{"line":72,"column":1}},"key":"Ze0HdetF3w"}],"key":"FRhtciZzLZ"}],"key":"HYXSu7weP3"}],"key":"G380bXqL44"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. The Nanosat Bridge (The Physical Link)","position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"key":"wW6aa4V19G"}],"identifier":"id-1-the-nanosat-bridge-the-physical-link","label":"1. The Nanosat Bridge (The Physical Link)","html_id":"id-1-the-nanosat-bridge-the-physical-link","implicit":true,"key":"IuJ3trs5du"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":75,"column":1},"end":{"line":75,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Modern Nanosats (3U to 12U CubeSats) act as Tactical Edge Nodes in orbit.","position":{"start":{"line":75,"column":1},"end":{"line":75,"column":1}},"key":"QxjBbUzm6H"}],"key":"HlAa0eN0XD"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":76,"column":1},"end":{"line":79,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":76,"column":1},"end":{"line":76,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Hardware: The Nanosat carries a Q-NET-compatible laser terminal or a high-frequency Ka-band radio.","position":{"start":{"line":76,"column":1},"end":{"line":76,"column":1}},"key":"hHFkUEuH8p"}],"key":"ltwVXPwjxz"}],"key":"pne4sCQOYZ"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":77,"column":1},"end":{"line":77,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Link: The MEG-fiber interface (worn by the user) transmits data to a local ground terminal (running your K3s/Go/Envoy stack). This terminal “uplinks” the encrypted neural stream to the Nanosat.","position":{"start":{"line":77,"column":1},"end":{"line":77,"column":1}},"key":"Bfzscx5DDS"}],"key":"sqhT2sc1e4"}],"key":"evjp93UxL3"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":78,"column":1},"end":{"line":79,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Q-NET Extension: Some Nanosats now perform Space-to-Ground Quantum Key Distribution (QKD). The satellite beams entangled photons down to the ground terminal, providing the “Quantum Seed” for your TLS 1.3 tunnel even in areas without physical fiber.","position":{"start":{"line":78,"column":1},"end":{"line":78,"column":1}},"key":"nE8gnoaEqg"}],"key":"DblB93EpS1"}],"key":"cHuljbuyte"}],"key":"LS7uZ49iIg"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":80,"column":1},"end":{"line":80,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. CSDAP Integration (The Data Layer)","position":{"start":{"line":80,"column":1},"end":{"line":80,"column":1}},"key":"tL24jaA3YX"}],"identifier":"id-2-csdap-integration-the-data-layer","label":"2. CSDAP Integration (The Data Layer)","html_id":"id-2-csdap-integration-the-data-layer","implicit":true,"key":"R0pVO8A2FX"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":1},"end":{"line":81,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"CSDAP is the NASA/DoD program that buys commercial satellite data (from companies like Planet, Spire, or BlackSky) for government use.","position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":1},"end":{"line":81,"column":1}},"key":"w4yVaLuhxb"}],"key":"yGd5sifnc5"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":82,"column":1},"end":{"line":85,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":82,"column":1},"end":{"line":82,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Contextual Awareness: CSDAP provides high-resolution imagery and RF signals from the user’s specific location.","position":{"start":{"line":82,"column":1},"end":{"line":82,"column":1}},"key":"l8U5exCFCe"}],"key":"gA8lkmXGBq"}],"key":"W4AfVnQLOx"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":83,"column":1},"end":{"line":83,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Fusion: Your Go-based microservice in the cloud merges the “Neural Stream” (what the user is thinking/feeling) with “CSDAP Data” (what the satellites see around the user).","position":{"start":{"line":83,"column":1},"end":{"line":83,"column":1}},"key":"JMrJpD02DE"}],"key":"WTh22sUIDe"}],"key":"r4Jvhve8pf"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":84,"column":1},"end":{"line":85,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example: If the user’s neural interface detects a high-stress “threat” response, the system automatically pulls the latest CSDAP SAR (Synthetic Aperture Radar) imagery of the surrounding 5km to identify potential hazards.","position":{"start":{"line":84,"column":1},"end":{"line":84,"column":1}},"key":"TnxImrKAd4"}],"key":"DR8rAPqhDT"}],"key":"StXNlokNXC"}],"key":"iBN4qZhSZq"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":86,"column":1},"end":{"line":86,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Implementing the “Space-Aware” Pod","position":{"start":{"line":86,"column":1},"end":{"line":86,"column":1}},"key":"cwRDJgiUH7"}],"identifier":"id-3-implementing-the-space-aware-pod","label":"3. Implementing the “Space-Aware” Pod","html_id":"id-3-implementing-the-space-aware-pod","implicit":true,"key":"qC89tfOWEF"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":87,"column":1},"end":{"line":88,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"To make this work, your K3s Pods must be “Space-Aware”:\nProtocol Optimization: Standard TCP/IP fails over satellite due to high latency. Your Envoy Wrapper is configured to use QUIC (UDP-based) or SCPS (Space Communications Protocol Specifications) to keep the neural stream fluid.","position":{"start":{"line":87,"column":1},"end":{"line":87,"column":1}},"key":"M2qx0SlE7p"}],"key":"pVvVWuWnaC"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":89,"column":1},"end":{"line":90,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":89,"column":1},"end":{"line":90,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Intermittent Connectivity: The Go driver uses a “Store and Forward” buffer. If the Nanosat passes behind a mountain, the MEG-powered interface stores the neural data in a local Sidecar and bursts it to the satellite once the link is restored.","position":{"start":{"line":89,"column":1},"end":{"line":89,"column":1}},"key":"eI0SUBC0Yn"}],"key":"VzW6S226WG"}],"key":"VZUkFCjrUj"}],"key":"VHsKhqxPbW"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":1},"end":{"line":91,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"4. Identity & Access (Entra ID in Space)","position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":1},"end":{"line":91,"column":1}},"key":"eG3RVWq7mG"}],"identifier":"id-4-identity-access-entra-id-in-space","label":"4. Identity & Access (Entra ID in Space)","html_id":"id-4-identity-access-entra-id-in-space","implicit":true,"key":"jy81MkBCBl"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":92,"column":1},"end":{"line":93,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":92,"column":1},"end":{"line":92,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cross-Domain Identity: Entra ID manages the permissions for the satellite uplink. The Nanosat verifies the user’s Workload Identity before allowing the data to enter the “Space Segment” of the DoDIN.","position":{"start":{"line":92,"column":1},"end":{"line":92,"column":1}},"key":"ZWG712CmMu"}],"key":"DC2JmxfUz1"}],"key":"j2nHAI79Gp"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":93,"column":1},"end":{"line":93,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stream Access: A commander at a HQ can view the “CSDAP + Neural” fusion dashboard. Think Neuralink with first person visual and subtitles. They authenticate via Entra ID MFA, and the Envoy Proxy decrypts the satellite-delivered stream in real-time.","position":{"start":{"line":93,"column":1},"end":{"line":93,"column":1}},"key":"RxF3YvrgKg"}],"key":"sDdmDVpFUy"}],"key":"HWuOwk8fWS"}],"key":"tfPlWGdQKc"}],"key":"aclaJSptoM"}],"key":"TaD5EXpBCG"},"references":{"cite":{"order":["Chung_2022"],"data":{"Chung_2022":{"label":"Chung_2022","enumerator":"1","doi":"10.1145/3502181.3531475","html":"Chung, J., Zacherek, W., Wisniewski, A., Liu, Z., Bicer, T., Kettimuthu, R., & Foster, I. (2022). SciStream: Architecture and Toolkit for Data Streaming between Federated Science Instruments. <i>Proceedings of the 31st International Symposium on High-Performance Parallel and Distributed Computing</i>, 185–198. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1145/3502181.3531475\">10.1145/3502181.3531475</a>","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3502181.3531475"}}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"Index","url":"/index-12","group":"Dashboard"},"next":{"title":"Biological Assets","url":"/bio-assets","group":"Dashboard"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3000"}